.TH SDL_SetWindowProgressValue 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetWindowProgressValue \- Sets the value of the progress bar for the given window’s taskbar icon.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetWindowProgressValue(SDL_Window *window, float value);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window whose progress value is to be modified\[char46]
.TP
.I value
the progress value in the range of [0\[char46]0f - 1\[char46]0f]\[char46] If the value is outside the valid range, it gets clamped\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

